    <string name="warning_private_dns">Android Private DNS is set to a specific hostname, so lookups from Chrome and other apps bypass this app. Set Private DNS to Off or Automatic in the network settings.</string>
    <string name="info_chrome_title">Notes for Chrome</string>
    <string name="info_chrome">If Chrome › Settings › Privacy and security › Use secure DNS is set to a custom provider, Chrome encrypts its DNS and sends it directly, so blocking will not work. Keep it on "Use your current service provider". Ads served from the same domain as the content (for example the YouTube app) cannot be blocked at the DNS level.</string>
